{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting","id":1414512,"title":"What are your opinions on Infernal Wish-granting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-18T23:54:32-07:00","id":1414512,"title":"What are your opinions on Infernal Wish-granting?","content":"So at lower levels, Infernal wish granting can give you dots of attributes and ability. At higher levels, you gain mutations and backgrounds. Wanna turn into the richest, most politically connected, most adored man in the world, with several Exalted allies? Sure! Just spend the willpower, and it'll be yours!<br /> <br /> Which, of course, cuts things out of the story. Getting to Resources 5, or Allies 5, or Influence 5, or other kinds of high level background dots can be entire sessions in and of itself. Just sitting there, letting it get granted is a bit... anticlimatic. And then there's the question of what's can you really do. You can just grant 5 dots of resources to anyone, and they have to do what you say. With 5 dots in abilities, attribues, and backgrounds, is there anything your newfound flunkies can't do together? At least, without dragging in gods, exalted, and everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T01:45:03-07:00","id":1414526,"title":"","content":"I <a href=\"https://youtu.be/nJ19zSF6Qs8?t=158\" target=\"_blank\">like</a> it.<br /> I <a href=\"https://youtu.be/L0P1A6p0MIk\" target=\"_blank\">love</a> it.<br /> I <a href=\"https://youtu.be/QDjiudUGI5o?t=43\" target=\"_blank\">want</a> more of it.<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish...&quot;<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> No story worth telling ends with the words &quot;I wish&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish&quot; is where the story <i>starts</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-19-2020, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T02:05:18-07:00","id":1414528,"title":"","content":"Hmm... If I really analyze it, I get the inspiration for the magic existing; Infernals are about taking on demon powers to infuse into Exalted Charms (in the same manner that Dragonblooded infuse elemental power or Sidereals fate power and so on). Demons or somewhat analoguous beings like jinns, in folk stories / myths are often bound to constrain their vast powers to perform wishes, in exchange for bargains.<br /> <br /> So I think that's the thematic base, but there needs to be some thought in 3e about much this actually works. As it is, I'm not sure it really works that well. 2e Infernals aren't bound to restrictions like the demons of folklore (part of their theme is in being *unbound* relative to the rest of hell). Maybe they should be in 3e, with a subtheme taking on more of the restrictions of demons and Yozi.<br /> <br /> Like, on another thought, in general, Infernals should be able to corrupt the mortals, etc. of Creation by offering them forbidden power, with strings attached. Should this be implemented by a specific bundled Charm though? Rather than a methodology for how they apply a broader power set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T02:15:13-07:00","id":1414529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414526#post1414526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No story worth telling ends with the words &quot;I wish&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish&quot; is where the story <i>starts</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>YOU. <br /> <br /> YOU.<br /> <br /> I LIKE YOUR STYLE","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T02:16:39-07:00","id":1414530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414528#post1414528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... If I really analyze it, I get the inspiration for the magic existing; Infernals are about taking on demon powers to infuse into Exalted Charms (in the same manner that Dragonblooded infuse elemental power or Sidereals fate power and so on). Demons or somewhat analoguous beings like jinns, in folk stories / myths are often bound to constrain their vast powers to perform wishes, in exchange for bargains.<br /> <br /> So I think that's the thematic base, but there needs to be some thought in 3e about much this actually works. As it is, I'm not sure it really works that well. 2e Infernals aren't bound to restrictions like the demons of folklore (part of their theme is in being *unbound* relative to the rest of hell). Maybe they should be in 3e, with a subtheme taking on more of the restrictions of demons and Yozi.<br /> <br /> Like, on another thought, in general, Infernals should be able to corrupt the mortals, etc. of Creation by offering them forbidden power, with strings attached. Should this be implemented by a specific bundled Charm though? Rather than a methodology for how they apply a broader power set.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing. A thing about exalted is the moral neutrality and greyness. <br /> <br /> There's no splat that's definitely evil and definitely good. That includes Infernals. Making Infernals be the kind of shit that would fit in Infernals Chapter 1 and 2 would miss the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T02:19:03-07:00","id":1414531,"title":"","content":"I think the wish-granting owes quite a bit more to Faust (with a few touches of The Godfather) than it does to jinn folklore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting#post1414512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can just grant 5 dots of resources to anyone, and they have to do what you say.</div> </div> </div> </div>They only have to do it once, though. The Infernal should choose wisely.<br /> <br /> I think the principle of the thing is pretty sound, but I think it could do with a bit more pizzazz than adding dots to traits.<br /> <br /> I also dislike the idea of an Infernal raising their own capabilities with it, but that's how I feel about every training power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T02:33:51-07:00","id":1414533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414531#post1414531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They only have to do it once, though. The Infernal should choose wisely.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't even HAVE to do it once, in the strictest sense. Though there's terrible concequences for not doing it... I imagine the average Infernal could kill a given mortal who defies them, regardless of wish granting powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also dislike the idea of an Infernal raising their own capabilities with it, but that's how I feel about every training power. </div> </div> </div>I disagree. It still costs XP, all you're doing is bypassing training time... which you could do anyway with a good story reason.<br /> <br /> My preference would be to see more training powers and less downtime. YMMV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414528#post1414528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Demons or somewhat analoguous beings like jinns, in folk stories / myths are often bound to constrain their vast powers to perform wishes, in exchange for bargains.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;They were Exalted, all except the Infernals who were of the jinn.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T02:46:33-07:00","id":1414534,"title":"","content":"There's nothing stopping an Infernal from forcing someone to swear loyalty to him with the threat of the vow, and then use variants of fealty acknowledging audience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 09-19-2020, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T03:30:11-07:00","id":1414535,"title":"","content":"Well, except for an ST telling them not to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T04:17:31-07:00","id":1414538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414530#post1414530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing. A thing about exalted is the moral neutrality and greyness.<br /> <br /> There's no splat that's definitely evil and definitely good. That includes Infernals. Making Infernals be the kind of shit that would fit in Infernals Chapter 1 and 2 would miss the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I guess folks could dispute that. Though sure, I wouldn't really suggest making them take inspiration from Infernals Chapter 1 and 2, but cos they suck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414533#post1414533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;They were Exalted, all except the Infernals who were of the jinn.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... There are Exalted whose powers include working under restrictions and ritual requirements. Sidereals do for'ex, and doesn't make them Pattern Spiders or Celestial Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T04:29:41-07:00","id":1414539,"title":"","content":"Isn't part of Exalted being 'saying a lot about morality by saying nothing about it'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T04:34:50-07:00","id":1414540,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean, I guess that the setting does and should shy away from declaring any set of characters evil (and particularly in some sense of having an &quot;elemental&quot; or &quot;essential&quot; evil) but that does not mean that they are prohibited from writing groups of characters - the Guild, the Realm, Nemissaries, the Fair Folk - that some set of their audience would view as &quot;evil&quot;. Though I don't know what that really has to do with my comment anyway tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T04:44:05-07:00","id":1414541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414540#post1414540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mean, I guess that the setting does and should shy away from declaring any set of characters evil (and particularly in some sense of having an &quot;elemental&quot; or &quot;essential&quot; evil) but that does not mean that they are prohibited from writing groups of characters - the Guild, the Realm, Nemissaries, the Fair Folk - that some set of their audience would view as &quot;evil&quot;. Though I don't know what that really has to do with my comment anyway tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more having a problem with this: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Infernals should be able to corrupt the mortals, etc. of Creation by offering them forbidden power, with strings attached.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Too much baggage with the wrods 'corrupt' and 'forbidden power'. <br /> <br /> If an Infernal looks at a poor farmer who swears loyalty to him, and then gives him Resources 5 in return, is that corruption or forbidden?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T04:49:21-07:00","id":1414543,"title":"","content":"OK; using those words purely to evoke fictional archetypes, no moral judgments really intended (I assume that it would be forbidden and corrupt in the eyes of Heaven, or the Immaculate Philosophy and other such in setting actors, of course!).<br /> <br /> But anyway, I guess the substance of my comment was a bit in agreement with your suggestion that having a power that simply granting traits like this &quot;<i>(O)f course, cuts things out of the story.</i>&quot; and that it would be more interesting and organic for Infernals to have a generalized set of powers they could use to raise a mortal to high station and wealth (for instance an Infernal good at socialize acts as their patron, effectively, etc.), and game and setting incentives to use them for that purpose, rather than a specific &quot;<i>Grant wishes for soul</i>&quot; power that cuts beside all that and works as an act of sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T05:18:20-07:00","id":1414547,"title":"","content":"I said it about \u201cevil\u201d in the Abyssals thread, I\u2019ll paraphrase it here.<br /> <br /> An Infernal\u2019s not \u201ccorrupt\u201d <i>because</i> he\u2019s an Infernal; he\u2019s literally engaging in corruption <i>because he\u2019s putting someone in power with the understanding that he\u2019ll be using his influence over that person to get later favors</i>.<br /> <br /> A Solar or a Dragon-Blooded or a mortal can do that too, and it would also be corruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-19-2020, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T05:24:42-07:00","id":1414548,"title":"","content":"Also the notion of genies being able to alter reality when carrying out the wishes of a master is more of a pop culture thing than a folklore or myth thing: the one bound in the lamp in the story of Aladdin didn\u2019t snap his fingers and turn Aladdin into a prince; he physically brought Aladdin a princess and <i>built</i> a palace for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-19-2020, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T05:36:34-07:00","id":1414551,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of people at the time tended to ignore the limitation of the Cecelyn charm as well. As far as Irecall, it was a wish granting charm but it was supposed to be limited by Cecelyn's theme of desolation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","name":"Plastic Doll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T06:43:15-07:00","id":1414555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414534#post1414534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing stopping an Infernal from forcing someone to swear loyalty to him with the threat of the vow, and then use variants of fealty acknowledging audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but she can also say &quot;Swear fealty to me or I'll kill you&quot;, then, like, casually break a tree in half.<br /> <br /> You don't need wishes for Fealty Acknowledging Audience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T06:59:11-07:00","id":1414556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414555#post1414555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but she can also say &quot;Swear fealty to me or I'll kill you&quot;, then, like, casually break a tree in half.<br /> <br /> You don't need wishes for Fealty Acknowledging Audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... are we actually disagreeing with one anohter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T07:28:29-07:00","id":1414560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting#post1414512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So at lower levels, Infernal wish granting can give you dots of attributes and ability. At higher levels, you gain mutations and backgrounds. Wanna turn into the richest, most politically connected, most adored man in the world, with several Exalted allies? Sure! Just spend the willpower, and it'll be yours!<br /> <br /> Which, of course, cuts things out of the story. Getting to Resources 5, or Allies 5, or Influence 5, or other kinds of high level background dots can be entire sessions in and of itself. Just sitting there, letting it get granted is a bit... anticlimatic. And then there's the question of what's can you really do. You can just grant 5 dots of resources to anyone, and they have to do what you say. With 5 dots in abilities, attribues, and backgrounds, is there anything your newfound flunkies can't do together? At least, without dragging in gods, exalted, and everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the concept, the execution has problems.<br /> <br /> Some Storytellers would treat it like a complete monkey's paw while others went the route that if you were paying xp for these out of nowhere backgrounds then having any complications associated with their sudden appearance was dumb. At the simulationist deep end, backgrounds in general just became another trait you could pump xp into and stuff would find its way to you... including artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T07:48:18-07:00","id":1414563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414548#post1414548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the notion of genies being able to alter reality when carrying out the wishes of a master is more of a pop culture thing than a folklore or myth thing: the one bound in the lamp in the story of Aladdin didn\u2019t snap his fingers and turn Aladdin into a prince; he physically brought Aladdin a princess and <i>built</i> a palace for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my main thing with wish granting in games. I don't like freeform reality-editing, but I'm all in favour of making the Infernal player actually figure out <i>how</i> to use their own occult might to make the streetrat into a prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3174-carl-ollivier","name":"Carl.ollivier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T08:10:11-07:00","id":1414566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414556#post1414556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... are we actually disagreeing with one anohter?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm agreeing with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T23:33:13-07:00","id":1414695,"title":"","content":"Usually in fiction wish granting creatures are depicted as being something like all-powerful, or at least with limits that are poorly defied and very high. What limits they do have tend to be more geared towards the manner of wishes that can be granted, like no wishing for more wishes, no killing the wishmaster, absolute ironclad binding on any deals etc. It's not necessarily a great place to have a point of view character in a story.<br /> <br /> On the other hand the concept of wishes is amazing. Even without the Wish spell in my last DnD campaign I had a devil constantly show up and tempt the players to make deals for things that were in his considerable power to grant. Sometimes they took those deals, and more than once they even turned the deal back on the devil.<br /> <br /> On the other-other hand the POV character for stories about wishes is basically never the wish granter. In the cases where it is, that character is usually kind of separated from their powers. Like they are bidden to grant wishes in certain cases, and that's not really where their agency is. Also there tend to be some no shenanigan rules like no wishing for more wishes, you only get one wish, no bringing people back from the dead. The reason being, obviously, if you just have characters with a bunch of unlimited wishes they just wish for everything which is dirt boring story resolution.<br /> <br /> All of this has to be consistent with RPG rules too. So the movie Aladdin has a lot of those traits, 3 wishes, no shenanigans, but there's no limit to the number of people that can have the lamp. At least none stated. You could just pass the lamp to Jasmine, Sultan, whatever trusted friends you know. Or, since Exalted is an RPG with social influence, just hammer some poor mortal with it to make them wish for whatever crap you wanted. The lamp becomes unlimited wishes in that scenario because of the way people play the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, so we have all that in mind, no shenanigans, limited number of wishes to keep stories focused on characters not wishes, no abusing workarounds, and I'll add on one here which is that the scope should be big. Rather than get one merit dot you should be able to wish for things like an entire army from nothing, or a dragon to guard your kingdom, things like that. Lastly, you probably shouldn't be allowed to leap ahead of other characters by hundreds of experience points, so keeping the pay xp for dots/charms should stay. You can learn every charm in an MA style, but you can't just get a whole MA for free.<br /> <br /> So what if we have these rules<br /> <br /> 1. Limit once per story. Can't use the charm more than once per story, unless reset by completing some kind of defining goal through use of a wish contract.<br /> <br /> 2. The scope of what can be changed is large, it can create geographical features like canyons or mountains, grant exaltation, enormous wealth, whatever. The other side of that, as the scale grows the chance for bad side effects also grows. If you are a mortal peasant and wish to become the Solar king of your nation you will suffer from almost certain doom.<br /> <br /> 3. Wishes must align with a character's intimacy. The greater the wish, the greater the intimacy it aligns with. You can regret the wish instantly, but some part of you really had to want it, not just say the words.<br /> <br /> 4. If you're changing stats on a player's character sheet, they must have the xp required for those changes.<br /> <br /> 5. Granting wishes is extremely taxing, the mote and willpower costs are very high, and for days afterwards the Infernal suffers from fatigue penalties.<br /> <br /> 6. Wishes can't be granted to characters that can grant wishes, and one character can't benefit from a wish more than once, barring very extreme circumstances.<br /> <br /> <br /> With all that I think you'd be good to go, but I probably missed something. Is should be generally a good framework to have characters that can grant incredible wishes that jumpstart a story, or let you totally change the direction of an existing story, but don't completely take over and make the entire story, and indeed setting, about stockpiling wishes, where wishes are the only real power in the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T01:54:48-07:00","id":1414702,"title":"","content":"...question. What was the point of that post?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T03:27:13-07:00","id":1414707,"title":"","content":"Seemed pretty clear to me; he was examining the fiction in which we encounter wish-granting entities (WGE), and trying to work out a set of rules that would allow WGEs to be characters that have agency but are still reasonably \u201cbalanced\u201d so the game doesn\u2019t just become about what happens when you can\u2019t make a wish because Shenron\u2019s cooldown timer is running.<br /> <br /> <i>That said</i>, I feel like sorcerous workings might already be a pretty good ruleset to crib from for WGEs, so I\u2019d prefer to just tweak how those work for Infernals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-20-2020, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T05:46:34-07:00","id":1414717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414707#post1414707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seemed pretty clear to me; he was examining the fiction in which we encounter wish-granting entities (WGE), and trying to work out a set of rules that would allow WGEs to be characters that have agency but are still reasonably \u201cbalanced\u201d so the game doesn\u2019t just become about what happens when you can\u2019t make a wish because Shenron\u2019s cooldown timer is running.<br /> <br /> <i>That said</i>, I feel like sorcerous workings might already be a pretty good ruleset to crib from for WGEs, so I\u2019d prefer to just tweak how those work for Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T07:07:34-07:00","id":1414728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414702#post1414702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...question. What was the point of that post?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't be passive aggressive.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T07:45:06-07:00","id":1414733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414728#post1414728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't be passive aggressive.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I&quot;m not being passive aggressive. I'm literally asking. Is this some kind of 'new way to make an infernal wish granting charm'? Is this 'here are the tropes used for wish granting entities'? <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">2. The scope of what can be changed is large, it can create geographical features like canyons or mountains, grant exaltation, enormous wealth, whatever. The other side of that, as the scale grows the chance for bad side effects also grows. If you are a mortal peasant and wish to become the Solar king of your nation you will suffer from almost certain doom.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit no, never, ever, grant Exaltation. Granting Exaltation is a terrible idea. Just look at the shit people get up to. No. Being able to manipulate who exalts is something I would not accept for any homebrew. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1. Limit once per story. Can't use the charm more than once per story, unless reset by completing some kind of defining goal through use of a wish contract.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit of a problem, isn't it? Doesn't this simply mean that you collapse the entire tree into one single charm? One single charm that you can only use once in a story? Doesn't this kinda fuck over Infernals who really wish to be the kind of person who grants wishes and uses it as debt? How about a charm that's wide-ranging (dear god no granting exaltation) to one character at a time, that fits in thematically? That way you can't just load up on bullshit (like a king with resources 5 and 5 dots in every single attribtue and ability) while also meaning that you can actually you know, grant wishes and use them as a method of social leverage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T08:08:07-07:00","id":1414737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414733#post1414733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I&quot;m not being passive aggressive. I'm literally asking. Is this some kind of 'new way to make an infernal wish granting charm'? Is this 'here are the tropes used for wish granting entities'?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't argue with Mods. Take an infraction.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T08:11:22-07:00","id":1414739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414695#post1414695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually in fiction wish granting creatures are depicted as being something like all-powerful, or at least with limits that are poorly defied and very high. What limits they do have tend to be more geared towards the manner of wishes that can be granted, like no wishing for more wishes, no killing the wishmaster, absolute ironclad binding on any deals etc. It's not necessarily a great place to have a point of view character in a story.<br /> <br /> On the other hand the concept of wishes is amazing. Even without the Wish spell in my last DnD campaign I had a devil constantly show up and tempt the players to make deals for things that were in his considerable power to grant. Sometimes they took those deals, and more than once they even turned the deal back on the devil.<br /> <br /> On the other-other hand the POV character for stories about wishes is basically never the wish granter. In the cases where it is, that character is usually kind of separated from their powers. Like they are bidden to grant wishes in certain cases, and that's not really where their agency is. Also there tend to be some no shenanigan rules like no wishing for more wishes, you only get one wish, no bringing people back from the dead. The reason being, obviously, if you just have characters with a bunch of unlimited wishes they just wish for everything which is dirt boring story resolution.<br /> <br /> All of this has to be consistent with RPG rules too. So the movie Aladdin has a lot of those traits, 3 wishes, no shenanigans, but there's no limit to the number of people that can have the lamp. At least none stated. You could just pass the lamp to Jasmine, Sultan, whatever trusted friends you know. Or, since Exalted is an RPG with social influence, just hammer some poor mortal with it to make them wish for whatever crap you wanted. The lamp becomes unlimited wishes in that scenario because of the way people play the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, so we have all that in mind, no shenanigans, limited number of wishes to keep stories focused on characters not wishes, no abusing workarounds, and I'll add on one here which is that the scope should be big. Rather than get one merit dot you should be able to wish for things like an entire army from nothing, or a dragon to guard your kingdom, things like that. Lastly, you probably shouldn't be allowed to leap ahead of other characters by hundreds of experience points, so keeping the pay xp for dots/charms should stay. You can learn every charm in an MA style, but you can't just get a whole MA for free.<br /> <br /> So what if we have these rules<br /> <br /> 1. Limit once per story. Can't use the charm more than once per story, unless reset by completing some kind of defining goal through use of a wish contract.<br /> <br /> 2. The scope of what can be changed is large, it can create geographical features like canyons or mountains, grant exaltation, enormous wealth, whatever. The other side of that, as the scale grows the chance for bad side effects also grows. If you are a mortal peasant and wish to become the Solar king of your nation you will suffer from almost certain doom.<br /> <br /> 3. Wishes must align with a character's intimacy. The greater the wish, the greater the intimacy it aligns with. You can regret the wish instantly, but some part of you really had to want it, not just say the words.<br /> <br /> 4. If you're changing stats on a player's character sheet, they must have the xp required for those changes.<br /> <br /> 5. Granting wishes is extremely taxing, the mote and willpower costs are very high, and for days afterwards the Infernal suffers from fatigue penalties.<br /> <br /> 6. Wishes can't be granted to characters that can grant wishes, and one character can't benefit from a wish more than once, barring very extreme circumstances.<br /> <br /> <br /> With all that I think you'd be good to go, but I probably missed something. Is should be generally a good framework to have characters that can grant incredible wishes that jumpstart a story, or let you totally change the direction of an existing story, but don't completely take over and make the entire story, and indeed setting, about stockpiling wishes, where wishes are the only real power in the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>So..... Why? <br /> <br /> Why? <br /> <br /> What for? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">2. The scope of what can be changed is large, it can create geographical features like canyons or mountains, grant exaltation, enormous wealth, whatever. The other side of that, as the scale grows the chance for bad side effects also grows. If you are a mortal peasant and wish to become the Solar king of your nation you will suffer from almost certain doom.</span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Holy shit no, never, ever, grant Exaltation. Granting Exaltation is a terrible idea. Just look at the shit people get up to. No. Being able to manipulate who exalts is something I would not accept for any homebrew.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">1. Limit once per story. Can't use the charm more than once per story, unless reset by completing some kind of defining goal through use of a wish contract.</span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is a bit of a problem, isn't it? Doesn't this simply mean that you collapse the entire tree into one single charm? One single charm that you can only use once in a story? Doesn't this kinda fuck over Infernals who really wish to be the kind of person who grants wishes and uses it as debt? How about a charm that's wide-ranging (dear god no granting exaltation) to one character at a time, that fits in thematically? That way you can't just load up on bullshit (like a king with resources 5 and 5 dots in every single attribtue and ability) while also meaning that you can actually you know, grant wishes and use them as a method of social leverage.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T09:58:39-07:00","id":1414753,"title":"","content":"One wish per person per story, no reset condition would work.<br /> <br /> Or one wish EVER per person, with achieving a Legendary Social Goal as a reset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T10:20:19-07:00","id":1414756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414753#post1414753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One wish per person per story, no reset condition would work.<br /> <br /> Or one wish EVER per person, with achieving a Legendary Social Goal as a reset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <br /> <br /> Because seriously. If you have this entire schtick and reduce it to a charm you can only use once per story... it's just way too cruel. <br /> <br /> And I say that if you can only use it so few times, then that means that you not only can do more than give a few dots of background and abilities (a better way is to remold them into some kind of template), you must also have a correspondingly mightier hold onto them. <br /> <br /> Like, say, as long as they keep their power you grant to them, they *must* obey you. No ifs. No buts. If they throw away what you gave them, they can be free again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T10:39:22-07:00","id":1414757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414756#post1414756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because seriously. If you have this entire schtick and reduce it to a charm you can only use once per story... it's just way too cruel.</div> </div> </div> </div>So maybe don't have it be something where it's your &quot;entire schtick?&quot; Like, Robin in my Sunday group has Wake the Sleeper, which is a once-per-story Charm and is <i>hella powerful</i>, but she does more than just wake up people's artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T10:42:21-07:00","id":1414758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414757#post1414757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So maybe don't have it be something where it's your &amp;quot;entire schtick?&amp;quot; Like, Robin in my Sunday group has Wake the Sleeper, which is a once-per-story Charm and is <i>hella powerful</i>, but she does more than just wake up people's artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't see why people who used to be social monsters in 2e might object? <br /> <br /> Like, you might as well go to a solar and say 'maybe you shouldn't be allowed to carry out big performance speeches or pen written attack'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T10:51:12-07:00","id":1414760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414758#post1414758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, you might as well go to a solar and say 'maybe you shouldn't be allowed to carry out big performance speeches or pen written attack'</div> </div> </div> </div>There's quite a bit of difference between performing a grandiose speech and gifting someone a palace from nowhere.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, there <i>are</i> social Charms with limits to how often you can use them, such as <b>Soul-Firing Performance</b>. It's not unreasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-20-2020, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T11:44:46-07:00","id":1414770,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, I would be very tempted to second Alucard's suggestion upthread (assuming he's getting the right impression from the post) and think it might be a good idea write Infernal wish magic to be just bonuses to Sorcerous Workings that use the wishes and dreams of Creation's inhabitants as part of their means, and bonuses to oathbinding on beneficiaries of Sorcerous Workings. And some more bonuses if the Infernal adds some &quot;evil genie&quot; twist... Add some flavour text about how borrowing the dreams and wishes of Creation's folk helps Infernals to smuggle their power in and overcome the wards that have been worked into Creation's structure against Yozi magic for Yozi ends (assuming that doesn't contradict anything!).<br /> <br /> Kind of just give the incentives for Infernal Sorcerers to go around Creation Fausting people, without actually having a specific Wish-Granting-Sorcery-That's-Not-Sorcery Charm / Charm Tree.<br /> <br /> (What are the compelling reasons this would kind of suck? ; ) )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T11:49:35-07:00","id":1414771,"title":"","content":"If the wish-granting Charm demanded a price...<br /> <br /> Like, a young Infernal cannot simply defer the price; the target must repay the wish immediately (or in a timely fashion) or suffer a curse equal to the gift. Deferring this effect indefinitely requires mastery or effort on the Infernal\u2019s part.<br /> <br /> With this kind of cost attached, the Infernal cannot grant her own wishes because the magic will not allow her to put her in debt to herself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T12:07:43-07:00","id":1414774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414756#post1414756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> <br /> Because seriously. If you have this entire schtick and reduce it to a charm you can only use once per story... it's just way too cruel.<br /> <br /> And I say that if you can only use it so few times, then that means that you not only can do more than give a few dots of background and abilities (a better way is to remold them into some kind of template), you must also have a correspondingly mightier hold onto them.<br /> <br /> Like, say, as long as they keep their power you grant to them, they *must* obey you. No ifs. No buts. If they throw away what you gave them, they can be free again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This really doesn't mesh with 3e's dynamics for social stuff. If you were to do this, I'd copy notes from a few homebrews and give them an intimicay with X uses to exploit. The infernals in 2e even had a requirement of &quot;can be exploited a number of times equla to dots&quot; I think, didn't they?<br /> <br /> My issue with wish granting honestly was that it felt...hollow. Like, in retrospect I can see how it's a cool aesthetic thing for the demonic champions (Hell, Solars can do empowering people with presence, wishes for infernals works!) but it was lacking...some of the flavor for me I guess. Like, we don't actually see that many wish granting demons in Malfeas (I guess the Dream Merchant?) and it felt very much &quot;Faustian bargain&quot; when Demons and Demon themes are rarely so mundane. <br /> That said! A demonic tutor unlocking forbidden powers in exchange for promises is totally cool. I could see it either mechancially as the Lore charms (which, note, instill a free intimiacy for solars already--there's precedent) or as Presence Empowering Shout Style charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T12:11:12-07:00","id":1414778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414770#post1414770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit, I would be very tempted to second Alucard's suggestion upthread (assuming he's getting the right impression from the post) and think it might be a good idea write Infernal wish magic to be just bonuses to Sorcerous Workings that use the wishes and dreams of Creation's inhabitants as part of their means, and bonuses to oathbinding on beneficiaries of Sorcerous Workings. And some more bonuses if the Infernal adds some &quot;evil genie&quot; twist... Add some flavour text about how borrowing the dreams and wishes of Creation's folk helps Infernals to smuggle their power in and overcome the wards that have been worked into Creation's structure against Yozi magic for Yozi ends (assuming that doesn't contradict anything!).<br /> <br /> Kind of just give the incentives for Infernal Sorcerers to go around Creation Fausting people, without actually having a specific Wish-Granting-Sorcery-That's-Not-Sorcery Charm / Charm Tree.<br /> <br /> (What are the compelling reasons this would kind of suck? ; ) )</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lunars get to convert people into beastfolk without needing to become sorcerers. To transform folks into animals. To conjure parts of themselves as spirits.<br /> <br /> And a few other methods of investing power into them.<br /> <br /> Wish-granting to me seems like one of those areas of Infernals that represents a very good cross-section between the ultimate cosmic power bit and engaging with people on a direct level based on appeals to their motives and attractions. A ripe element to focus on that demonstrates Abilities in form and function as a solid foundation to engage in demonic and Primordial activity.<br /> <br /> Lunars get to do witch stuff with their own Charms. I'd need to check back to see what the standard for frequency is, but it's still there.<br /> <br /> We were also always told that one of the things that would set Infernals apart from Solars structurally was a more direct and over-the-top form of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T12:22:48-07:00","id":1414779,"title":"","content":"I think there's a distinction there in that you would want that particular ability you highlight under conversion to beastfolk separate from sorcery both for thematic reasons - it's an outgrowth of Lunar Essence, not sorcery - and for established setting facts and play motivations - Lunars generally raise Beastmen armies, whatever their general competencies and areas of focus; they are not the Exalted-Of-The-Moon-Who-Are-Mysteriously-Unable-To-Spawn-Beast-Children-Unless-They-Are-Also-Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Those are less strong aspects with Infernals and this particular trick and trope (having Beastmen armies is a core Lunar thing since day one, and this is... less so), so I'm fairly relaxed about either option - either going with it as an adjunct to sorcery to avoid proliferation of further subsystems and because it feels part of Infernal Occult and goes well with being an Infernal Sorcerer, or booting it up under another one of their Ability trees (Lore or something, perhaps) to add variation of feel. You could really go either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T12:25:25-07:00","id":1414781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414739#post1414739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So..... Why?<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> What for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, probably should have lead with that. You asked &quot;What's your opinion of Infernal Wish Granting?&quot; my answer is that compared to what I think wishes should be it's super weak. I can only wish for dots on my character sheet, I can only get one at a time, and for background dots it takes WEEKS? If I don't have an army, and I want a command 5 army, it takes 15 weeks, and 5 applications of that charm. That's lame, especially since in Dungeons &amp; Dragons my wizard can look at an approaching enemy army, realize nobody here has any way to defend themselves and speak the words &quot;I wish for an army of my own to match this invading force&quot; and BAM I have it, right there, as soon as I say the words it's mine.<br /> <br /> Amazingly though, the infernal one is also more easy to abuse than Wish, because there's very few limits on how often it can be used, and who it targets. So like, you have a bunch of people theorycrafting that you kidnap a young impressionable person, an just sit around in the wilderness using nearly irresistible social influence to make them a mortal god with 5s in every attribute, ability and background, who now owes you hundreds of favours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414739#post1414739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit no, never, ever, grant Exaltation. Granting Exaltation is a terrible idea. Just look at the shit people get up to. No. Being able to manipulate who exalts is something I would not accept for any homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usurping the Unconquered Sun in selecting his own chosen is maybe a touch too far, but granting <i>an</i> exaltation I don't think is. Like you can't make somebody a Solar, but you can make them some other kind of similar exalt. If it's limited to once per story so you're not making them everywhere, and sometimes people won't wish for Exaltation anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414739#post1414739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bit of a problem, isn't it? Doesn't this simply mean that you collapse the entire tree into one single charm? One single charm that you can only use once in a story? Doesn't this kinda fuck over Infernals who really wish to be the kind of person who grants wishes and uses it as debt? How about a charm that's wide-ranging (dear god no granting exaltation) to one character at a time, that fits in thematically? That way you can't just load up on bullshit (like a king with resources 5 and 5 dots in every single attribtue and ability) while also meaning that you can actually you know, grant wishes and use them as a method of social leverage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah you can have charms that build up to this one, but they need to be even more limited in what they can grant and what you can ask in return. Like you give a king a dot of strength, you can't then ask that he give up his throne to you a week later. If you tack a Willpower cost onto it should be pretty okay, that way you can't just take an army and turn them all instantly into the Legion of Silence.<br /> <br /> There might have to be special considerations for Exalts though, because giving a Solar 5s in every ability changes things a lot more. The other side of that being having a Solar indebted to do absolutely anything for you is a hell of a good deal.<br /> <br /> I'd also probably say keep the merits out of it, except ones like pain tolerance and mutations. Making things like income or contacts or influence appear out of nowhere is a lot bigger on the reality editing side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T12:47:00-07:00","id":1414784,"title":"","content":"Question are we talking about the Cecylne wish charms from 2e or something I apparently missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T13:07:09-07:00","id":1414786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414784#post1414784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question are we talking about the Cecylne wish charms from 2e or something I apparently missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI believe the intention is a hypothetical 3e version of said Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T14:32:27-07:00","id":1414818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414786#post1414786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI believe the intention is a hypothetical 3e version of said Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, wanted to be sure before opinion since the OP comment talks about it in the progression that sort of mirrors the progression of the Cecelyne charms from 2e. And my opinions on that go abit differently than what I would want from a 3e version.<br /> <br /> Though I personally find JohnDoe's comment about it only working once a story with no reset or once ever well stupidly overcompensating for a perceived danger since the abilities aren't nearly powerful enough for those sort of balances to be necessary unless you just declare the Infernal's ability to grant wishes is closer to one of the Dread Power Rituals from Magnus Archives or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 09-20-2020, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T16:06:52-07:00","id":1414838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414818#post1414818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I personally find JohnDoe's comment about it only working once a story with no reset or once ever well stupidly overcompensating for a perceived danger since the abilities aren't nearly powerful enough for those sort of balances to be necessary unless you just declare the Infernal's ability to grant wishes is closer to one of the Dread Power Rituals from Magnus Archives or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but also go back and look at JohnDoe's suggestions about awesome stories that start with &quot;I wish...&quot; I'll add some of my own.<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish the goblins would come and take you away, right now.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish you and your entire family would kiss my ass and be my slaves.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish Buffy the vampire slayer had never come to this town.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish for you to make me a prince.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish I was a real boy.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish I was never born.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish I could see dinosaurs for real.&quot;<br /> <br /> If we're saying infernals have the power to grant wishes, but also that this power is weak enough that it's 100% okay to be spammed over and over again then I don't want it, or don't want to call it wish granting anyway. Again, I refer to DnD, which is magnitudes more epic in its ability to grant wishes.<br /> <br /> Out of all those wishes up there the Infernal can't even use the 2e ones to grant them. The closest you get is &quot;make me a prince&quot; and that takes months and months, and dozens of applications of the charm. When I say to the Devil &quot;Make me a prince&quot; I want to be marching down the streets of Agrabah with seventy-five golden camels, elephants, an entire zoo of exotic pets and god knows what else by the next day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T17:24:12-07:00","id":1414844,"title":"","content":"I feel like Demon the Descent has a good way of doing it. Like there are mechanics in play so certain wishes will be granted without the Demon needing to do anything. So person making a pact for strength will start getting stronger once the pact is sealed even if the Demon just leaves and doesn't do anything. However, there's also the option for the Demon to just use their own abilities to grant wishes if they want more control over how its handled or a faster handling on the time table. Example a person making a pact with a demon for a million dollars could just wait for the universe to start mucking around and such until the person has acquired the million or if the Unchained has access to that kind of wealth they can literally just pop down the suitcase full of bills, bullion, gems, or cut them a check. Now granted the Unchained have to list their end of the deal up front, even if part of it was a favor to be named later, but I feel like Infernals doing the wish thing probably would make more sense in the Mephistopheles and Faust roles than the Genie in Disney's Aladdin.<br /> <br /> Plus I like the idea having the option grant wishes my own way. Farmer wishes to be a prince, signs the deal next day finds various demons, elementals and what have you building their manor/keep/castle etc; the infernal hands them a certificate of nobility or what have you and offers to negotiate for an army to defend their territory or acquire more should those be fitting to the new noble's ambitions. (I personally always loved the Aladdin Musical at Disneyland where the Genie responded to Jafar wishing to be Sultan by tapping him pronouncing him Sultan and then snarking for a couple minutes.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T20:38:31-07:00","id":1414872,"title":"","content":"I won't have issues with the Infernal giving gifts and doing favors and holding them over the target's head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T00:52:15-07:00","id":1414883,"title":"","content":"One of the problems perhaps specific to Exalted where characters have lots of other capabilities and means, would be about introducing a very powerful specific wish power, for use in response to wishes by others (which I think has been mooted upthread), is where the power steps above what a their party can achieve by other means. That seems like it would lend itself to gamified manipulations, where some characters gets an external servant to wish for something which they want. Cute if it's a one off or infrequent, but I think it would feel a bit strange in a longer term, which could feel kind of fake.<br /> <br /> Probably part of my motivation here to argue (tentatively) for Internals to be incentivized to engage in wish granting behaviour, but have no dedicated wish power and use their general capabilities to achieve the end, to avoid that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T02:35:33-07:00","id":1414887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414838#post1414838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but also go back and look at JohnDoe's suggestions about awesome stories that start with &quot;I wish...&quot; I'll add some of my own.<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish the goblins would come and take you away, right now.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish you and your entire family would kiss my ass and be my slaves.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish Buffy the vampire slayer had never come to this town.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish for you to make me a prince.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish I was a real boy.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish I was never born.&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish I could see dinosaurs for real.&quot;<br /> <br /> If we're saying infernals have the power to grant wishes, but also that this power is weak enough that it's 100% okay to be spammed over and over again then I don't want it, or don't want to call it wish granting anyway. Again, I refer to DnD, which is magnitudes more epic in its ability to grant wishes.<br /> <br /> Out of all those wishes up there the Infernal can't even use the 2e ones to grant them. The closest you get is &quot;make me a prince&quot; and that takes months and months, and dozens of applications of the charm. When I say to the Devil &quot;Make me a prince&quot; I want to be marching down the streets of Agrabah with seventy-five golden camels, elephants, an entire zoo of exotic pets and god knows what else by the next day.</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words, you want wide-scale shaping and reality-warping effects? That would be a huge pain to balance and write out. And also really fucking story-breaking. <br /> <br /> Like, Buffy is the protagonist. What kind of charm just lets you smash apart entire quests by themselves. Yes, Infernals can do that. But there's a difference between 'I can make you richer and more politically powerful' and 'I just snapped my fingers and yeah, that questline is gone'. <br /> <br /> And how are you going to scale it? Ok, you have like... a mortal hero who really hates your infernal and wants to tear down all he does. He's a mortal sorcerer and is murdering your cult like wheat being cut down by a scythe. What's the cost for removing him? What about an Essence 5 solar with a slight dislike of Creatures of Darkness and is a melee supernal and can cut you in half with a single blow? What about a dragonblooded brotherhood who is coming here and might kill you if they see you? By this point, the entire thing is mostly based on Storyteller Fiat. What's a tyrant lizard ally? Or a sudden Kukla rampage? Or a sudden thunderstorm that hits your enemies? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Out of all those wishes up there the Infernal can't even use the 2e ones to grant them. The closest you get is &quot;make me a prince&quot; and that takes months and months, and dozens of applications of the charm. When I say to the Devil &quot;Make me a prince&quot; I want to be marching down the streets of Agrabah with seventy-five golden camels, elephants, an entire zoo of exotic pets and god knows what else by the next day.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I see no issue with higher level costs being incurred in exchange for solid goods and immediate results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T02:35:45-07:00","id":1414888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414779#post1414779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are less strong aspects with Infernals and this particular trick and trope (having Beastmen armies is a core Lunar thing since day one, and this is... less so)</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the history of Infernal Exalted in the setting, this is an argument that could be used to invalidate basically every possible way of expressing them, so I don't think it's a very strong one.<br /> <br /> In deciding what capabilities for the Green Sun Princes are iconic enough to return and refine, the only thing we have are the parts of their late Second Edition hardback that people responded strongly to. By what I've seen these last nine odd years, some variation on the wish granting powers is included there.<br /> <br /> If we focus on what Infernals have had for the same length of time as Lunars, well, there's not much to do around the piece of setting lore of them being employed as honour guard for the Ebon Dragon's nuptials. Besides, social interaction by way of Faustian bargain does not strike me as this huge stretch for how to realise an Exalt that needs to be both demonic and reminiscent of Solars; actually seems kind of basic. Kind of have a stronger basis for that than they do the green fire.<br /> <br /> In any case, I find even myself to be focusing a bit too much on the side where they have much power to grant things (even if I think that should ultimately be a distinct part of it). That the key iconic side is in the ties of obligations this can create towards the Infernal. The image of them standing there with outstretched arm while the air swirls with green energy, and the impression that binding the agreement with a handshake is maybe not the best idea.<br /> <br /> Combined with a bit of appropriate showmanship to draw people in.<br /> <br /> <i>You have a dream you wish to tell.<br /> And it's just laughable, but hey kid what the hell.<br /> 'Cause you're one of a kind, a charming demon belle.<br /> Now let's give these burning fools a place to dwell.</i><br /> {take it boys}<br /> <br /> I must admit that at a moment such as this, I see one of the limitations of mediating powers via Charms. Chronicles of Darkness Changelings get a whole dedicated sub-system to manage their procedures of supernatural deal-making, but Exalted books seem to lack much space for such things (and what Infernals might spare probably needs to be reserved for constructing their shintais).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T03:12:21-07:00","id":1414890,"title":"","content":"&quot;Basically every possible way&quot; seems a bit extreme reduction (there are core ideas there), but yeah I do see how 3e Devs should write Internals as relatively unconstrained by 2e's implementation, given the degree to which their design diverges.<br /> <br /> Though in any case, to gently remind though we're (you and I) are here not really discussing whether &quot;some variation on the wish granting powers&quot; (we've established no real disagreement on that, nor really on imagery!), as you possibly note, but whether it would fit best as integrated with the sorcery system and other social interactions, or as a stand-alone separate system created by Charms (presumably in another ability than Occult).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T03:23:57-07:00","id":1414892,"title":"","content":"Actually I'm in agreement with Isator at least about the obligation part. That's more important to me than how the Infernal is granting the wisher a kingdom, which is why I suggested the reality-warping be accomplished via sorcerous workings (an already fairly freeform system), but I'd fully want the bit where you owe them afterward and the various ways the Infernal can use that, to be represented with Infernal Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T03:46:19-07:00","id":1414894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414892#post1414892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I'm in agreement with Isator at least about the obligation part. That's more important to me than how the Infernal is granting the wisher a kingdom, which is why I suggested the reality-warping be accomplished via sorcerous workings (an already fairly freeform system), but I'd fully want the bit where you owe them afterward and the various ways the Infernal can use that, to be represented with Infernal Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Sorcerous workings are freeform. <br /> <br /> I think the exp debt should be on the wisher. Not the granter. And also, its faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T03:54:41-07:00","id":1414895,"title":"","content":"Alucard, sure (though I don't think that contradicts any statement I made about what I thought you might be arguing for ; ) ). <br /> <br /> I don't think there's any disagreement with me and you on that point either (that Internals should have some sort of Charms that can bind subjects to obligations, and that these should interact with a &quot;wish granting&quot; Charm that works through the sorcery system was, I think in my post last page!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T06:09:35-07:00","id":1414908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414883#post1414883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the problems perhaps specific to Exalted where characters have lots of other capabilities and means, would be about introducing a very powerful specific wish power, for use in response to wishes by others (which I think has been mooted upthread), is where the power steps above what a their party can achieve by other means. That seems like it would lend itself to gamified manipulations, where some characters gets an external servant to wish for something which they want. Cute if it's a one off or infrequent, but I think it would feel a bit strange in a longer term, which could feel kind of fake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where? <br /> <br /> I mean, what can the infernal wishing charm get that other characters can't get on their own? Resources 5? Simple for any exalt. Influence 5? Well, it takes some effort, but yeah, you can get it in-play. Followers 5? Just throw in an excellency and you'll get yourself an army of followers. Attributes and abilities? They can train them up. <br /> <br /> All wish-granting does is make it so that its easy to obtain, and a lot more faster. And then there's the EXP debt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T07:32:04-07:00","id":1414911,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a>, I'm responding to the tangent by DrLM about possibilities of stronger, once per story (or otherwise infrequent) wish magic. I agree that the existing Charms are not so powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T07:51:06-07:00","id":1414915,"title":"","content":"*puts head in hands* <br /> <br /> Ok, how did we get here again? I think it was because I was asking if Infernal charms cut out too many plot points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T09:59:23-07:00","id":1414934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414915#post1414915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*puts head in hands*<br /> <br /> Ok, how did we get here again? I think it was because I was asking if Infernal charms cut out too many plot points?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well my thought was that you left it a bit open ended on whether you were talking about the existing 2e charms for infernal wish granting, or a hypothetical of 3e's versions and what was wanted and well that's always fun ground.<br /> <br /> Oh amusing thing when I checked Verdant Emptiness Endowment, the condition imposed the wisher had a few clauses that made it a case that they were no longer obligated to the infernal for said wishes free of charge. First was if the request proved impossible for the wisher, the other was if it took a month or longer. Which I just find funny, not that I ever saw the penalty of Essence # botches a particularly intimidating threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T10:13:10-07:00","id":1414937,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I'm talking about if it invalidated or made redundant certain aspects of PC's journeys. After all, if you wish to be king of the threshold, you can just skip the concept of getting fame, gathering followers, getting to know all the important people, just by wishing for Follower, Influence, and Contact background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T10:31:51-07:00","id":1414938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414937#post1414937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I'm talking about if it invalidated or made redundant certain aspects of PC's journeys. After all, if you wish to be king of the threshold, you can just skip the concept of getting fame, gathering followers, getting to know all the important people, just by wishing for Follower, Influence, and Contact background.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I mean it did only work at one dot at a time and still cost xp for it. So, if you wanted to be king of the threshhold you and ST would have needed to agree on which merit(s) constitute ruling the threshold and you'd need sufficient xp to get each of those dots (each upgrade lists that the charm fails if the subject is still in xp debt for any reason) so I mean honestly it feels like a thing you'd be conquering the threshhold manually while waiting for the charm's effects to kick in since each dot also took weeks to kick in.<br /> <br /> Plus the fact that the charm specifically mentioned it worked by forcing crap into the loom the cheesed off the pattern spiders more than normal always struck me as just begging for intervention, extermination, and bad things to happen when if the same target keeps getting hit with these good fortune hacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T14:18:58-07:00","id":1414968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1414512-what-are-your-opinions-on-infernal-wish-granting?p=1414838#post1414838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;I wish I could see dinosaurs for real.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;...And so, from that day onward, DrLoveMonkey couldn't help but, when setting eyes upon a bird, clearly and without fail, see how all of their features had come from flightless, non-avian theropod antecedents. And also cursed the genie for being a pedantic cheapskate, among other phrases, each more lively with their anger than the last.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T16:30:55-07:00","id":1414988,"title":"","content":"The complication in 3rd edition is not so much Verdant Emptiness Endowment, which could be transferred over relatively easily but the additional features granted by Bestowal of Accursed Fortune since unlike 2nd edition backgrounds 3rd edition Story Merits cannotbe purchased with experience.<br /> <br /> This is also when the effects of the charm at wish granting start to feel really lame. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T14:33:54-07:00","id":1415737,"title":"","content":"While continuing to think about the topic, I must admit that I find it walks a very fine line. When I think of emphasizing it as a process of being able to fulfil wishes, I can't help but imagine an Infernal that gets to bring things about while skipping over the interesting process, which actually feels like it narrows things down. But speculating on an emphasis on binding people to what they owe in repayment also feels like... it's not just that it seems a bit prosaic, but shifts the significance towards it being a means of getting other people to do things for you.<br /> <br /> It makes me think that... empowering people to the effect of adding traits, mutations, special powers should be a capability of Infernals, but spun off into its own conceptual space that has more in common with what the akuma bargain has been. If something is filling the narrative space of granting wishes, I feel as though that should be limited to arrangements of circumstance in a manner similar to some of the capabilities of Sidereals; it's not about a person desiring themselves to be different, but wanting something changed in the way of the world and their place in it. The kind of thing that can be expressed in Merits, but is not limited to them and where the greater focus is on the process bestowing them.<br /> <br /> So it could be something in which there's a capacity to modify the world that is fine-tuned enough to not overwhelm a bunch of other things the Infernal might need to do, but still captures the essence of a wish-granting narrative. Things that don't get overtly transformed, but shifts to reflect the desires of another.<br /> <br /> A bit similar to Solar prophetic Charms, but where the necessary input is the yearnings of a human soul rather than some kind of practical research, more demonic in character and cultivating different kinds of relationship.<br /> <br /> And still open to a level of abuse where the Infernal is the one who cultivates the yearnings that they then fulfil.<br /> <br /> As for the price to be paid... I'm feeling that it could be not just about providing for the Infernal, but it serves as some kind of function that seals the pact, and so needs to be symbolically relevant to that function. A bit like the sacrifices that Ligier's crafts require, and with a similar penalty for failure or refusal to provide; what you were granted but did not pay for twists horrifically against you.<br /> <br /> In that way, I could see still having a capacity for Infernals to grant their own wishes, but with some reservations about doing so; you don't quite consciously decide your own payment for it, and it may be that putting yourself in that position is ill-advised. So that's another possible dimension to granting the wishes of others; you manipulate them towards wanting what you want, but the burden of it lies upon their soul, and the price gets to be something that serves your interests as well to boot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}